          "text": "{\"relation\":\"MATCH\",\"consensus_summary\":\"Cedar primarily signifies strength, majesty, lofty and enduring stature, with that grandeur applied contextually to the righteous, divinely established kingship, imperial power, or pride destined for judgment.\",\"book_summary\":\"Cedar signifies towering power, height, and majesty rather than one fixed person or moral identity; it can represent Assyria, the Davidic house, or the righteous.\",\"consensus_core_identification\":\"Impressive strength and lofty, majestic stature whose specific bearer and moral value depend on context.\",\"book_core_identification\":\"Towering power and majestic stature that can belong to different bearers rather than denoting a fixed identity.\",\"core_relation\":\"EQUIVALENT\",\"extension_relation\":\"SAME_CASES\",\"boundary_disagreement\":\"No material boundary disagreement. The book highlights Assyria, Davidic rule, and the righteous, all already covered by the consensus. Its omission of durability, temple use, and ritual purification does not clearly reject those secondary associations.\",\"material_contradiction\":\"None. Both readings treat cedar as a multivalent image whose stable feature is lofty greatness rather than a single fixed referent.\",\"rationale\":\"Reduced to their minimum cores, both identify cedar with majestic height, strength, and stature, variably embodied by righteous people, royal or messianic power, and imperial greatness. The book's statement that cedar does not have one fixed identity closely matches the consensus emphasis on contextual multivalence. Differences are chiefly emphasis and selectivity, not a changed identification or material reclassification.\",\"citation_support\":\"STRONG\",\"strongest_objection\":\"The book foregrounds towering power and stature while the consensus also includes durability, flourishing, temple dignity, and purification. This could look like a narrowing, but the entry does not expressly exclude those secondary associations, and its cited applications substantially coincide with the consensus core.\",\"confidence\":\"high\"}"
        }
